<template><main>
  <header class="hero page-width"><div class="venue-pill">{{paper.venue}} · PROJECT PAGE</div><h1><span>{{paper.title}}</span>{{paper.subtitle}}</h1><p class="summary">{{paper.summary}}</p><div class="authors"><a v-for="author in authors" :key="author.name" href="#">{{author.name}}<sup>{{author.mark}}</sup></a></div><div class="affiliations"><span><sup>1</sup> Tencent</span><span><sup>2</sup> National University of Singapore</span><span><sup>3</sup> The Hong Kong Polytechnic University</span></div><div class="author-notes"><span>♣ Research internship at Tencent</span><span>* Corresponding authors</span><span>♦ Project leader</span></div><nav class="link-row" aria-label="Publication links"><a v-for="link in links" :key="link.label" :href="link.href" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"><span>{{link.icon}}</span>{{link.label}}</a></nav></header>
  <section class="page-width hero-media" aria-label="Paper teaser"><figure class="teaser-figure"><img :src="baseUrl + 'h3-world-teaser.jpg'" alt="H3-World teaser showing diverse visual environments"><figcaption><strong>H3-World</strong> enables character and camera control across diverse visual environments.</figcaption></figure></section>
  <section class="page-width section" id="demo"><div class="section-heading"><span>01</span><div><h2>Interactive world-control demos</h2><p>H3-World follows camera and character actions across diverse, open-ended visual environments.</p></div></div><div class="demo-grid"><article v-for="(demo,index) in demos" :key="demo.label" class="demo-card"><div class="demo-visual"><span class="demo-index">0{{index+1}}</span><video :src="baseUrl + demo.video" controls autoplay muted loop playsinline preload="metadata">Your browser does not support HTML video.</video></div><h3>{{demo.label}}</h3><p>{{demo.note}}</p></article></div></section>
  <section class="paper-section" id="abstract"><div class="page-width text-layout"><div class="side-label"><span>02</span> ABSTRACT</div><div><h2>Abstract</h2><p class="abstract-lead">We introduce <strong>H3-World</strong>, an action-controllable world model that turns keyboard input into temporally grounded video control.</p><p>Built by fine-tuning MiniMax-H3 on gameplay footage, H3-World converts character and camera actions into a short English instruction for every video latent frame. These instructions are injected through the pretrained text pathway and aligned to their corresponding frames with a directed attention mask, enabling precise action-to-motion binding without adding action-specific trainable modules.</p><p>Only a rank-32 LoRA is trained on the self-attention projections. This lightweight adaptation produces controllable motion from the same initial frame under different action sequences, while supporting longer-horizon generation and generalization across diverse visual environments.</p><div class="highlight"><span>KEY TAKEAWAY</span><strong>Language-aligned action control enables a single world model to translate keyboard inputs into coherent, controllable video dynamics.</strong></div></div></div></section>
  <section class="page-width section" id="method"><div class="section-heading"><span>03</span><div><h2>How H3-World works</h2><p>H3-World aligns language descriptions of keyboard actions with video latents, then adapts the pretrained H3 transformer with a lightweight LoRA.</p></div></div><figure class="method-figure"><img :src="baseUrl + 'h3-world-method.png'" alt="H3-World method diagram"><figcaption><strong>Figure 1.</strong> H3-World packs visual tokens and latent-aligned action language into one sequence. A directed attention mask binds each action description to its corresponding visual latent, while LoRA adapts the H3 self-attention projections.</figcaption></figure></section>
  <section class="paper-section" id="temporal-control"><div class="page-width section"><div class="section-heading"><span>04</span><div><h2>Temporally specified control</h2><p>H3-World follows different camera instructions at different moments within the same video.</p></div></div><figure class="method-figure"><img :src="baseUrl + 'h3-world-temporal-control.png'" alt="Temporal control comparison"><figcaption><strong>Figure 2.</strong> The instruction requests a sharp left pan in the first half and a sharp right pan in the second half. Global prompting provides coarse motion but misses the scheduled switch. The frozen per-latent interface remains nearly static. <strong>H3-World follows both actions in their requested time intervals.</strong></figcaption></figure><div class="control-summary"><div><strong>Global prompt</strong><span>Responds to motion, but not to the full schedule.</span></div><div><strong>Per-latent, no LoRA</strong><span>Has the interface, but produces almost no motion.</span></div><div><strong>H3-World</strong><span>Controls action direction and when each action happens.</span></div></div></div></section>
  <section class="page-width section citation" id="citation"><div class="section-heading"><span>05</span><div><h2>BibTeX</h2><p>If you find this work useful, please consider citing it.</p></div></div><div class="bibtex-card"><button @click="copyBibtex">{{copied?'Copied ✓':'Copy BibTeX'}}</button><pre>{{bibtex}}</pre></div></section>
